# ─── SECRETS — never commit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds live SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR / GROQ / GEMINI / OPENROUTER keys.
# citation/apikey.env is a SECOND credential file — found only by an explicit
# pre-commit scan, not by the obvious `.env` pattern. Both are excluded by name
# AND by the catch-all patterns below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.env
**/apikey*
*.key
*secret*
*credential*

# ─── COPYRIGHTED PAPER PDFs — do not redistribute ───────────────────────────
# The corpus is 20 published papers; 10 are paywalled (IEEE/Springer/Elsevier/ACM).
# papers/manifest.csv carries the DOIs and access status so anyone can obtain them
# legitimately. fetch_corpus.sh downloads the open-access subset.
*.pdf
papers/*.pdf
bulk-download/

# ─── Large regenerable artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
# prompts.jsonl regenerates from the parsed HTML; graphml regenerates from triples.json.
output/*/kg/*/*/prompts.jsonl
output/*/kg/*/*/*.graphml
output/**/*.graphml
output/*/no-llm/
output/*/fast/
output/acl/
output/global_kg/
summary/

# ─── Finetuning / Q&A eval (Session 32) ─────────────────────────────────────
# These carry FULL paragraphs of the (partly paywalled) papers, like prompts.jsonl
# above, or adapter weights. Keep split.json / manifest.json / *_papers.txt /
# run_manifest.json / report.json tracked — they are what makes a run reproducible.
# ** not * : the consensus variant nests one level deeper (ft_data/consensus/fold0/train.jsonl),
# which a single-level pattern does NOT match. Session 35 found that file unignored.
ft_data/**/train.jsonl
ft_data/**/dev.jsonl
ft_data/**/parts/
ft_runs/*/adapter/
ft_runs/*/checkpoints/
ft_runs/*.cmd
qa_eval/*/questions.jsonl
qa_eval/*/qgen_raw.jsonl
qa_eval/*/rejected.jsonl
# Pipeline step markers are machine-local: a fresh clone carrying base_gen/train .done
# files would make run_ft_pipeline.py SKIP those steps on the new machine.
ft_runs/_pipeline_*/*.done

# ─── C2/C5 judging bundles print WHOLE PARAGRAPHS of the papers (Session 34) ─
# The verdicts.csv / index.csv / replies next to them are kept; only the inputs are
# excluded (regenerable with `ontology_eval.py paragraphs`, and in the private bundle).
ontology_eval/*/*/paragraphs/*_batch_*.txt

# ─── Session scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ontology_eval_backup_*/
verdict_backup_*/
before_filter.json
ceo_before.json
*.log
chat_upload/
judge_upload/

# ─── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# derived from requirement.txt by the command in SETUP_NEW_MACHINE.md section 3; a committed
# copy could only go stale
req_no_torch.txt

# stray archives
*.zip

# stale session backups
output_backup_*/
triples_open/
